# secrets
.env

# Ingestion intermediates only. These are regenerable with load.py and chunk.py,
# and are never read at query time. Comments are kept on their own lines: a rule
# carrying a trailing comment is legal but easy to misread, and this file is the
# only thing standing between your Groq key and a public repo.
data/raw/
data/logs/
data/chunks.jsonl
data/*_dump.txt

# data/chroma/ and data/docs/ are deliberately NOT ignored. A deploy serves from
# a fresh clone, so the committed vector index and the *.meta.json files (which
# carry the corpus date shown in the answer footer) are what let the app boot
# with a working index and no network access at build time. ~2 MB total.

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# editors / os
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
